From 41c5d0f967d33e6d89b24295fb6f40fed0436f22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruilin Gao <ruiling@andrew.cmu.edu>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [rollout] feat: tool parser for the DeepSeek-V3 family
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DeepSeek-V3 family (V3, R1, V3.1, V3.2) writes tool calls with the
<｜tool▁calls▁begin｜> / <｜tool▁call▁begin｜> markers; V3 and R1 add the call
type and a fenced JSON block, V3.1 and V3.2 write "name<｜tool▁sep｜>{json}".
verl had no parser for either layout, so a tool loop with these models never
saw a tool call. Register DeepSeekV3ToolParser as "deepseek_v3": both layouts,
parallel calls, invalid JSON kept verbatim for the loop's existing handling.
---
